  "notes": "Nine-Year Continuous Basic Education (from 2017): Grades 1–6 primary and Grades 7–9 lower secondary, with the PSAC assessment at the end of Grade 6. Grades 10–11 lead to the Cambridge School Certificate and Grades 12–13 to the Higher School Certificate. Some learners take Grades 7–9 over four years in the Extended Programme. The former names (Standard I–VI, Form I–V, Lower and Upper Six) are aliases."
